frida: Quick mobile follow-up from yesterday's console smoke test — two odd things on narrow screens: 1) when the soft keyboard appears (search focus) the sticky header overlaps content and the first row gets hidden under safe-area notch. 2) swipe-to-close gesture for the left nav sometimes triggers row-swipe actions in the table. Screenshot/gif: https://img.redwood.test/console/2026-05-keyboard-overlap.gif

omar: Repro on iPhone SE simulator. Keyboard pushes viewport but our `position: sticky` header doesn't respect `env(safe-area-inset-top)` and we set `top: 0` which is wrong. Also the left-swipe gesture has a 40px conflict zone with row actions.

neel: For the sticky header: try adding `top: constant(safe-area-inset-top)` / `top: env(safe-area-inset-top)` fallback and compute header offset when keyboard opens (listen to visualViewport API). Quick patch: `header.style.top = visualViewport.offsetTop + 'px'` on focus.

pat: Gesture conflict: we should prioritize navigation gestures over row-kebab swipes when user starts from the left 24px edge. But that could hurt discoverability. Alternative: make table row swipe area start at 36px from right edge (kebab) and require a longer delta for swipe-to-open nav. Thoughts? :thinking:

frida: Prefer not to break discoverability. Maybe do edge-swipe for nav only when gesture starts from left edge (<20px) and keep row swipe as is. Also show a subtle affordance on the left edge to hint nav.

omar: Sounds good. Implementation sketch: add a pan handler with `touchstart` point check: if `clientX < 20` then treat as edge-nav; otherwise table swipe. Also add `touch-action: pan-y` on table rows to avoid horizontal gesture capture unless intent is clear.

neel: Regarding keyboard overlap: visualViewport gives us `visualViewport.height` and `visualViewport.offsetTop`. We should set a `--kv-viewport-offset` token and use that in CSS for sticky calculations. Fallback: recalc on `resize` and `orientationchange`. Example:```js
function updateHeaderOffset () {
  const offset = window.visualViewport ? window.visualViewport.offsetTop : 0;
  document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--kv-viewport-offset', offset + 'px');
}
visualViewport && visualViewport.addEventListener('resize', updateHeaderOffset);
```

pat: Accessibility nit: when keyboard opens we must ensure focus is not hidden under sticky header; screen reader users should still land on the input. Also update `aria-describedby` on the search input to mention "search results appear below" so NVDA/VoiceOver doesn't get lost.

frida: Table overflow: in stacked narrow layout long model IDs are still forcing horizontal scroll when the virtual keyboard is up. Suggest `max-width` + `word-break: break-word` on `.token` fields and collapse long strings into a pill with `title` attribute and a copy button. Also ensure toast copy works when keyboard present.

omar: CSS example to avoid overflow:```css
.token { max-width: calc(100% - 56px); overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; word-break: break-word; }
@media (max-width: 420px) { .stacked-row { display: block; } }
```

neel: UX copy: change "Show columns" -> "Columns & density" and in mobile sheet add helper line: "Choose visible columns and row density (saved per-device)". Also change the copy-to-clipboard tooltip from "Copied" to "Copied model ID" so it's clearer in multi-copy flows.

pat: Hit target note: ensure row tap target >=44px when stacked. For compact rows add `min-height: 44px` and make the whole row `role=button` with `aria-label` that reflects primary action. Keep kebab as separate `button` with `aria-haspopup`.

frida: Quick experiment idea: run 7-day A/B: Variant A = edge-swipe nav + standard row swipe; Variant B = no edge-swipe, show explicit nav hamburger. Metrics: accidental swipe rate, time-to-nav, task completion (open project). We'll recruit 8 participants for usability.

omar: Dev tasks: 1) add visualViewport adjustments + CSS token, 2) gesture discrimination (clientX < 20 edge), 3) token truncation + copy pill, 4) update breakpoint tokens in design tokens file.

neel: I'll own accessibility checklist and landing PR notes: focus management, aria labels, keyboard behavior when modal/sheet open, and screen reader readback for copied content.

ux-qa-bot: Reminder: update sources/design/tokens.md and add testcases to sources/slack/product with screenshot artifacts. Add e2e test for visualViewport behavior if possible.

pat: I'll prototype the gesture handler and a small demo. Posting link in a bit. Thanks all :thumbsup:
